  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Connecting Communities:Learning for Life</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A quarter of 15-24 year-olds in Zambia have never been to school. Many orphans, especially girls, don&#x2019;t finish basic education or go to high school.   This project trains committees to identify 14-16 year-olds not in school and those who may drop out. Some of the vulnerable young people work with the committees to set up clubs that provide business skills, homework help, drama and sports activities. Together, they lobby for better government services. The neediest families get help with school fees, materials and are supported to develop initiatives for them to earn money.   As a result and with the support of parents and the wider community more young people finish school. They and their families have more chance of work.</narrative>
  </description>
